{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791802162,"nonce":"LGyK8IuVozTmpeHJo7TokjMcojI=","title":"Add consistent Size variants to the remaining form controls and Badge","message":"Sizing audit after NumberInput ffc482f: Input, Textarea, Select, Combobox, InputOtp, Checkbox, RadioGroup, Slider and Badge lack the shared Sm/Md/Lg density API. Prioritize Input/Select/Combobox for aligned form rows, then Textarea/InputOtp, then Checkbox/RadioGroup/Slider/Badge. Size font, padding, glyphs, slots, tracks and thumbs together while preserving behavior, hit targets and theme shape tokens. For RadioGroup set size on the group and inherit it into items. Textarea sizes should express padding/type/minimum height without replacing developer-controlled dimensions. Table, Accordion, TreeView and menu rows warrant a separate density discussion instead of generic surface scaling. Existing Button, Toggle, ToggleSwitch, Tabs, Avatar/AvatarGroup, Progress, Spinner, Breadcrumb, Pagination and Kbd already have size variants. Dialog/Sheet/Drawer sizes express surface dimensions, not control density.","files":null}]}